                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Scudamore studied in London and Edinburgh, graduating MD in 1814 and shortly afterwards obtaining his license from the Royal College of Physicians. He was an expert on gout 
and   practised mostly in London.</p>
                        <p>Godwin's first entry is to Sir C Scudamore. The frequency of the visits and the
      links to Mary Wollstonecraft-Shelley suggest that she had arranged for Scudamore to see her father. </p>
